    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: on successful owner create, enqueue a welcome notification via the logger named `NOTIFY`, with a line containing the owner id and memberId.\n\nI followed the existing pattern where the controller calls `ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner)` after a successful create \u2014 that logic lives in a dedicated `OwnerAuditor` component with its own `AUDIT` logger. Rather than bloating the auditor with unrelated notification concerns, I added a parallel single-responsibility component:\n\n- **`WelcomeNotifier`** (`service/WelcomeNotifier.java`) \u2014 a small `@Component` that owns the `NOTIFY` logger and emits the welcome line carrying `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 injected `WelcomeNotifier` via the constructor and call `welcomeNotifier.welcome(owner)` right after `ownerAuditor.ownerCreated(owner)` in `addOwner`, so it fires only on a successful create (creation exists only in V1; V2 only lists).\n\nThe test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the log confirms the emitted line: `NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
